    "language": "en",
    "version": 1,
    "caption_draft": "System overview. (1) TLC Parquet files are cleaned into CSV tiers and (2) written to HDFS, whose 128 MB blocks are spread over the N workers. (3) run_job.sh submits a job to the ResourceManager, which (4) starts map/reduce tasks or a Spark executor next to the blocks; (5) intermediate pairs are shuffled between workers and (6) the merged output is checked and timed. The same image and the same mapper/reducer code run on 1-4 containers on one host and on Azure VMs.",
    "open_questions": [],
    "notes": "Brief confirmed by the user with defaults (single column, accent on the shared job code, Azure as a second deployment strip, no cache-experiment scripts). JobHistory dropped from the master row to keep the single-column budget; it is named in the text. Worker N is mirrored (tasks on the left) so the shuffle crosses the ellipsis gap in a straight line (nsdi24-023_fig3 lesson)."
  },
